# Context And Session Management

## Context Health

- Use full file paths in plans, review reports, and final reports.
- Summarize key constraints before complex multi-step work.
- Refresh context when the task changes between requirements, feasibility, proposal, detailed design, standards work, and review.
- If answer quality degrades or the same issue fails twice, stop and reassess context before continuing.

## Session Strategy

For large tasks, split work into independently verifiable sessions:

| Session | Goal | Persistence |
|---|---|---|
| 1 | Understand documents, scope, and constraints | Notes, rules, or document map |
| 2 | Draft or revise document content | Tracked document changes |
| 3 | Independent review and verification | Review findings and verification notes |

## Document Map

Large document repositories should maintain a lightweight `DOCUMENTS.md` at the project root:

```text
# Document Map
## Requirements
- docs/prd/              - PRD and SRS documents
## Feasibility
- docs/feasibility/      - feasibility studies and approval material
## Design
- docs/design/           - proposals, high-level designs, detailed designs
## Standards
- docs/standards/        - standards drafts, references, review comments
## Do Not Edit Directly
- published/             - approved baselines
```

The map should describe top-level structure only. Detailed constraints belong near the documents they govern.

## Noise Exclusion

Keep generated files, exports, build artifacts, third-party content, and temporary files out of routine search scope unless they are the review target.

## Configuration Iteration

Review agent configuration every three to six months or after major model releases. Separate rules that compensate for model limitations from rules that encode durable project conventions.
